<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15138" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕdessa</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔδεσσα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city of Macedonia</i>, <i>the
				burial-place of the kings</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 45,
			29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 7, 1, 7</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Edes-saeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Edessa</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antiphilus (dux),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					42, 51</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city of Mesopotamia</i>, <i>in the
				province of</i> Osrhoëne, now <i>Rhoa</i> or <i>Orfa</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 24,
				21, § 86</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12,
				12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 20, 11, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">21, 7, 7</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">and where Caracalla died,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
					Vict. Epit. 21</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Eutr. 8, 11</span></i>. —Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Edessēnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
			Edessa</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sepulcra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 18, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
